  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A disk of radius R rotates about its axis with angular speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\omega\"></span>. Point X is at a distance of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{2}\"></span> from the centre and point Y is on the circumference.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What are the ratios of the linear speeds and the centripetal acceleration of X to Y?</p>\n<p>The linear speed of X is v<sub>X</sub> and its acceleration is a<sub>X</sub>; the linear speed of Y is v<sub>Y</sub> and its acceleration is a<sub>Y</sub>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
  },
